WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.629
I'm at a party, taking just a couple minutes out to tell you that gold

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:06.750
has an E number. E numbers are the numbers given by the

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.700
European Food Safety Group -- or whatever -- and gold is technically

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.460
a food additive. You can have it for
decoration or -- you know, in little

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.740
drinks or something like that. You can also get it in this form: you can get it as gold leaf.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.859
And this is--well for gold, it's quite cheap. Each sheet

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:25.449
costs about £1 and that is because it's so unbelievably thin:

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:29.189
less than a micron. It's been rolled and rolled and rolled and

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:32.790
flattened and put into this little
booklet. And, uh...

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.630
Well, that means you can do all sorts of things with it but one thing you can do is

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:41.219
with a bit of luck...you can...
Got to be really careful here because--

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:44.649
--Do you want to just get a close shot of that?
And so, with a bit of luck

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:47.489
I should be able...

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.240
I have gold plated my tongue for about £1.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.860
And that is something you might not have known.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.720
-Ah! That does not taste good.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:12.150
-Does anyone else want a go? I've still got one left.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.450
And yes, since you asked that, it's pretty much going to go

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.450
unaltered, through me.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.440
[Translating these subtitles? Add your name here!]

